  "body": "Currently TAO (Timing-Allow-Origin) is checked as part of the CORS mechanism.\r\nHowever, for iframes it needs to be checked at the end, relative to the containing document's origin.\r\nImplementations already do this.\r\n\r\nI wonder how to go about it spec-wise:\r\n- To create a variant of `Finalize and Report timing` that does this, receiving an origin\r\n- Export some internals of the TAO check and let HTML do this when reporting an iframe (I think I prefer this, and it's closer to implementations)",
